# Git branch naming

Working branches: `<type>/<short-description>` (`feat`/`fix`/`hotfix`/`chore`/`refactor`/`docs`/`test`/`ci`/`build`/`perf`). Single trunk: `main` is the only long-lived branch. Hotfixes are ordinary short-lived `fix/*` (or `hotfix/*`) branches that fix-forward to `main` — there is no protected `release/*` branch. `claude/*` is reserved for AI web sessions. Enforced by `.husky/pre-push` (owner: **[be-code-quality-guard](../skills/be-code-quality-guard/SKILL.md)**).

## Deriving the name

`<type>` is the change's conventional-commit type, matching `BRANCH_TYPES` in `.husky/pre-push`. `<short-description>` is kebab-case, 2–5 words, ≤ 40 chars, naming the change itself — never a ticket id, a date, or a session slug. Keep it aligned with the commit subject and the PR title.

| Change | Branch |
| ------ | ------ |
| Fix British spelling in a doc | `docs/american-spelling-organization` |
| Add `POST /billing/invoices` | `feat/billing-invoice-route` |
| RLS scope bug on `webhook_event` | `fix/webhook-event-rls-scope` |
| Bump Fastify to 5.3 | `chore/bump-fastify-5-3` |

## AI web sessions: rename before the first push

Claude Code web assigns `claude/<platform-slug>` (e.g. `claude/session-request-wx3euu`) before the container boots. That slug is generated platform-side and **cannot be configured from this repo** — no file here changes it.

The cloud git proxy accepts a push to *any* branch name, but **rejects every form of delete** (`git push --delete`, `git push :ref`, and `DELETE /git/refs/...` → 403). So a `claude/*` branch that has already been pushed cannot be cleaned up from inside the session. Rename before the first push and the throwaway name never reaches the remote:

```sh
git branch -m <type>/<short-description>      # rename in place, BEFORE any push
git push -u origin <type>/<short-description>
```

If it is already pushed as `claude/*`, leave it — it auto-deletes when the PR squash-merges. Never open a second PR just to correct a branch name.
